# The exact denial each document in insecure.yaml must produce.
# scripts/test-policy-fixtures.sh compares this whole set: a message that
# disappears is a weakened rule, a message that appears is an unreviewed
# denial. File-level rejection alone hides both.
Pod denied must disable ServiceAccount token automount
Pod denied must not use hostNetwork
Pod denied must run as non-root
Pod denied must use RuntimeDefault seccomp
Pod denied must use only ServiceAccount naranjo-online
Service denied must be ClusterIP
Service denied must not declare externalIPs
container denied image must use an approved registry and full digest
container denied must declare a cpu limit
container denied must declare a cpu request
container denied must declare a memory limit
container denied must declare a memory request
container denied must disable privilege escalation
container denied must drop ALL capabilities
container denied must not be privileged
container denied must not declare a hostPort
container denied must use a read-only root filesystem
container denied must use the canonical image repository for namespace naranjo-online
container denied-init image must use an approved registry and full digest
container denied-init must disable privilege escalation
container denied-init must drop ALL capabilities
container denied-init must not be privileged
container denied-init must use a read-only root filesystem
container denied-init must use the canonical image repository for namespace naranjo-online
